Tests used to validate this implementation:

- `TestRandomAgainstBruteForce`: 1,200 random PBQP instances up to 6 nodes,
  domains up to 3, random `Inf` entries, and negative benefit edges. Solver
  cost must exactly equal brute force.
- `TestRandomRAAgainstBruteForce`: 300 random SSA/register-class/affinity
  instances. Builds PBQP, compares `Allocate()` cost against brute force, and
  checks fixed registers, class restrictions, and interference constraints.
- `TestBranchDoesNotPruneNegativeBenefits`: regression for the subtle negative
  benefit pruning bug. A K4 instance has optimum `-80`; pruning on partial
